timecrate (3.1.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Stage the PQ escrow secret and unwrap hybrid kits in the quarterly
    recovery guest before signature verification.
  * New application icon (blue crate with clock emblem), shipped as PNG at
    512/256/128 px in place of the scalable SVG.
  * Recovery drill now unwraps hybrid (ML-KEM) kits through the common
    reader instead of decrypting them raw, which failed every PQ kit.

 -- Norvi <apt@globalentry.systems>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:30:00 +0000

timecrate (3.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Google Drive direct sign-in: `remote connect --provider drive` runs the
    OAuth flow into a dedicated rclone config, and the window offers Drive
    as a first-class destination with the existing folder picker.
  * Post-quantum hybrid kits: TIMECRATE_CRYPTO=hybrid wraps each new kit
    in an ML-KEM-1024 envelope (OpenSSL) around the unchanged signed GPG
    kit. Classic kits stay readable; the escrow sheet carries both
    secrets and can be downloaded as TXT or PDF.

 -- Norvi <apt@globalentry.systems>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

timecrate (3.0.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The quarterly capstone decrypts the kit on disk instead of /tmp, which
    is a small tmpfs on Ubuntu 26.04, and fails when the kit is not
    authenticated or does not extract whole, instead of passing it as
    unsigned. A missing package sample, package selections or desktop
    settings fail the run too. The guest reboots itself for the reboot
    check, a forced stop and start tells a guest that cannot boot from a
    hypervisor that lost track of it, and the alert lists every failure.

 -- Norvi <apt@globalentry.systems>  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

timecrate (3.0.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * First public release, under the name Timecrate. Kits written by earlier
    versions are read, verified, restored and pruned as one series with new
    ones. Alerts go to a command of your choice, include lines may be globs,
    and the timers are enabled on installation and kept across upgrades.

 -- Norvi <apt@globalentry.systems>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
